  "body": "It has been brought up in https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1562547 that for pinned tabs, Firefox violates the rules for following hyperlinks, by opening targetless cross-origin links in a new tab instead of in the pinned tab itself. This is intentional behavior in Firefox, to lock pinned tabs at their original domain. I believe the spec should allow this kind of deviation from the default behavior.",
